      "sequence_position": 1,
      "problem": "Consider the two sets of $6$ paired observations shown in the table below.\n\n| **$\\,{x}_{i}\\,$** | $123$ | $122$ | $121$ | $120$ | $125$ | $127$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| **$\\,{y}_{i}\\,$** | $102$ | $111$ | $110$ | $105$ | $106$ | $108$ |\n\nCalculate ${S}_{xy}.$",
      "worked_solution": "Given a set of $n$ paired observations ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}$ and ${y}_{1},{y}_{2},…,{y}_{n},$ ${S}_{xy}$ is the sum of products of the deviations of ${x}_{i}$ and ${y}_{i}$ from their respective means, that is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{xy} & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})({y}_{i}-\\overset{―}{y}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we calculate the sample means $\\overset{―}{x}$ and $\\overset{―}{y}:$\n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{x}=\\frac{123+122+121+120+125+127}{6}=123\n$$\n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{y}=\\frac{102+111+110+105+106+108}{6}=107\n$$\n\nNext, we calculate the differences between the ${x}_{i}$ and $\\overset{―}{x}$, ${y}_{i}$ and $\\overset{―}{y}$, and their product.\n\n| **$\\,{x}_{i}\\,$** | $123$ | $122$ | $121$ | $120$ | $125$ | $127$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| **$\\,{y}_{i}\\,$** | $102$ | $111$ | $110$ | $105$ | $106$ | $108$ |\n| **$\\,({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})\\,$** | $0$ | $-1$ | $-2$ | $-3$ | $2$ | $4$ |\n| **$\\,({y}_{i}-\\overset{―}{y})\\,$** | $-5$ | $4$ | $3$ | $-2$ | $-1$ | $1$ |\n| **$\\,({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})({y}_{i}-\\overset{―}{y})\\,$** | $0$ | $-4$ | $-6$ | $6$ | $-2$ | $4$ |\n\nTherefore, ${S}_{xy}$ is\n\n$$\n{S}_{xy}=0+(-4)+(-6)+6+(-2)+4=-2.\n$$",
